{"id":"chatcmpl-02009aee-d73f-4a4a-a52d-8c73d550c686","object":"chat.completion","created":1795246655,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task required interpreting a medical image to distinguish between two lateralized diagnoses (right vs. left scoliosis). The successful strategy combined a targeted expert-model query about the specific feature (curvature direction) with an explicit verification step to guard against laterality/orientation errors. The key abstraction is: ask a focused feature-extraction question, then independently confirm the spatial/lateral interpretation before committing to an answer.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When options differ only by a lateralized attribute (left vs. right), query the model specifically for the direction/orientation of the relevant feature rather than asking for the diagnosis directly.\",\n    \"Insert a verification step whenever the answer hinges on spatial orientation, to confirm the feature's direction is interpreted relative to correct patient anatomy (not image mirroring).\",\n    \"Decompose the decision into a feature-extraction sub-question (describe the curvature) followed by a mapping step (convexity direction -> right/left diagnosis).\",\n    \"Use a domain-expert tool with a narrowly scoped question to reduce ambiguity when the distinguishing signal is a single localized feature.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Ask for the specific anatomical feature and its direction/orientation; confirm laterality against patient-side conventions before answering.\",\n    \"Binary lateralized classification\": \"Convert the choice into a directional feature query, then map the observed direction to the correct option label.\",\n    \"Ambiguous single-signal tasks\": \"Isolate the one discriminating feature, extract it explicitly, and verify it independently before finalizing.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the extracted feature's direction is stated relative to patient anatomy (right/left), not image coordinates.\",\n    \"Re-check that the mapped option label matches the observed direction (convexity right -> 'right ... scoliosis').\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":465,"total_tokens":857,"completion_tokens":392,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":465},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":392}}}